# The voyage itself: wonder, home, ship life, the dark, the approach.
# Arc, threads and plants: content/STORY_BIBLE.md (spoilers). Voice: content/STYLE.md.
# Personal threads: each `who ow_*` opener casts a different astronaut (`!is`), and
# that astronaut carries the thread to its payoff and epilogue line.

# --- Leaving -------------------------------------------------------------------
card p_live_call
type beat
cat human
due
once
days 1 1
roles A
text {A} calls home while the delay is still under a second. Someone tells a bad joke and {A} laughs on the beat, in real time, with everyone at the table. Afterwards {A} writes down who was there and what they ate, and folds the list into a flight-suit pocket.
do who ow_list A
do morale A 5

card p_music
type beat
cat human
due
once
days 2 2
roles A
when !is A ow_list
text {A} plays the same four bars on a travel guitar at the end of every watch, into the fleet channel, never the rest of the song. By the last top-off tanker six ships are guessing at the fifth bar, six different ways.
do who ow_song A
do trait A warm 1

card l_reboot
type beat
cat life
clue core
due
once
days 3 9
roles A
text The galley screen on {A}'s ship takes a 2.3-gigabyte update overnight and restarts at breakfast: the logo, a progress bar, the three-note chime, all over before {A} has counted to eleven. Then it logs out again. By departure the whole fleet is humming the chime.
do morale A 1
do who abort_who A

card l_dock_hello
type beat
cat life
clue core
due
once
days 12 12
roles A
text Crossing window. The next ship's hatch takes a code that goes stale in a fifth of a second. The procedure still says to read them up via the ground. {A} does, once: CODE STALE. Ship to ship it opens first time, and {A} files a correction to page two.
do trait A curious 1

card p_garden_plant
type beat
cat life
due
once
days 4 4
roles A
when !is A ow_list
when !is A ow_song
text {A} plants the garden: six seed pods in a tray the size of a laptop, under a lamp the colour of a plum. {A} labels each pod in tiny capitals and says good night to them on an open channel. Several people say good night back.
do who ow_garden A
do var garden 1

card l_manifest
type beat
cat life
clue core
due
once
days 5 7
roles A
text {A} reads the manifest like a shopping list: water on Cargo 3, rover on Cargo 4. Write-offs: a grey relay, "thruster stuck open"; the last window's hopper, "tipped, beacon intermittent"; Cargo 2, drill spares, "lost on landing, scar on a survey frame"; socks, "reason unknown".
do trait A curious 1

card l_departure
type beat
cat wonder
due
once
days 6 6
roles A
text The last tanker undocks at dawn. Seven ships light their engines for the departure burn, and {A} feels weight come back for the first time since launch. From here the flight log keeps one page for every five days, and by the next page {A} can hide Earth behind a thumb.
do morale A 3

card l_transfer
type beat
cat life
due
once
days 2 2
roles A
text The ships hold formation a few kilometres apart. One seat a ship, so no one failure takes two people, and the next ship reads back every critical command. Every few days they close up: a tethered line, after a morning of prebreathe. {A} has the first crossing and already calls it "educational".
do trait A brave 2

card l_handshake
type beat
cat life
due
once
days 12 20
roles A
when !is A ow_list
when home A
text The galley screen on {A}'s ship has started to sulk: after every restart it sits on its logo longer than it used to, then boots with a sad cloud icon and the word OFFLINE. {A} files a ticket titled "manners".
do morale A 1

# --- Thread: the list ------------------------------------------------------------
card p_list_letter
type beat
cat human
due
once
days 18 19
roles A
when is A ow_list
text The delay has turned calls into letters. {A} records one for home and talks straight through the gaps, then deletes it and does it again with pauses, which is worse, and then a third time at speed, list and all, which is the one that goes. The list from the first call is still in the pocket.
do morale A 2
do trait A warm 2

card p_packer_note
type beat
cat human
due
once
days 16 17
roles A
when flag stash_kept
when is A stash_who
when !flag stash_exposed
text A voice note from the Starbase loading crew reaches {A}, a forklift beeping behind it. The one with the Sharpie: "Eat the good rations first. The bad ones keep. And say hello to the hardware for us. It sulks if no one does." {A} checks the locker. True.
do morale A 2

card p_packer_note_g
type beat
cat human
due
once
days 16 17
roles A
when !is A ow_list
when !flag stash_kept
text A voice note from the Starbase loading crew reaches {A}, a forklift beeping behind it. The one with the Sharpie: "Eat the good rations first. The bad ones keep. And say hello to the hardware for us. It sulks if no one does." {A} checks the galley log: the good rations went first, fleet-wide. True.
do morale A 2

card g_news
type event
cat grim
due
once
days 27 28
roles A
when is A ow_list
text A message from home for {A}: a funeral, already over, for the neighbour who always brought the folding chairs, a name from the first call's list. By the time it arrived, everyone in the photos had gone home and changed. {A} watches the recording to the end and asks for the next watch.
do morale A -8
do trait A warm 3

card c_list
type beat
cat human
due
once
days 35 36
roles A
when is A ow_list
text {A} copies the list from the first call into the entry notes, name by name, and reaches the end feeling it's short. It is: the person who held the phone up that night never made it onto the list, because they were holding the phone. {A} adds them at the top.
do morale A 3

card a_list
type beat
cat arrival
due
once
days 42 42
roles A
when is A ow_list
text {A} writes to every name on the list from the first call, one more to the name that isn't there any more, and a last one to a loading bay at Starbase. Each will land eight minutes after it's sent. {A} sends them without a single pause: no ums, no gaps, no saving the good bit for last.
do morale A 3

# --- Thread: the song ------------------------------------------------------------
card p_song_ask
type beat
cat human
due
once
days 21 22
roles A B
when is A ow_song
text On the night {B} finally asks about the four bars, {A} plays them again, all four, and stops. "Planet first." {B} says that's a deal, and starts humming a made-up fifth bar on purpose.
do bond A B 5
do bond B A 3

card c_song
type beat
cat human
due
once
days 36 37
roles A
when is A ow_song
text Alone, with the channel off, {A} tries a fifth bar after the four and gets it wrong. Then wrong again, differently. {A} puts the guitar back in its bag. "Not yet," {A} tells the guitar. "Entry morning."
do trait A warm 1

card a_song
type beat
cat arrival
due
once
days 42 42
roles A
when is A ow_song
text On the last morning before the air, with a planet under the fleet again, {A} plays past the four bars, all the way through, and this time on the channel. Six ships hear the fifth bar at last: it falls where they all had it rising, and lands on the last note of the galley chime. "That's the one," {A} says.
do morale A 5

# --- Thread: the garden ------------------------------------------------------------
card p_garden_tend
type beat
cat life
once
days 8 20
weight 10
roles A
when is A ow_garden
text {A} waters the garden tray with a syringe, two millilitres per pod, and checks each one under the lamp. Nothing yet. {A} writes it down: "Nothing yet. Good, even nothing." Then tells the pods so.
do var garden 1

card p_garden_fail
type beat
cat grim
due
once
days 18 19
roles A
when is A ow_garden
text Four of the six pods have gone soft and grey: drowned. The schedule came from a book written for windowsills, where water drains away. Up here it just sits. {A} lifts them out with tweezers. "Wrong book," {A} tells the tray. "Let's go again." Half a dose, now, for the other two.
do morale A -3
do trait A warm 2

card p_garden_tend2
type beat
cat life
once
days 21 29
weight 8
roles A
when is A ow_garden
when !flag water_rationed
when !fired water_fail
text {A} waters the last two pods morning and night, and has started reading the seed packet's small print for encouragement. There isn't any, so {A} reads them the planting depth instead, with feeling.
do var garden 1

card p_garden_sprout
type beat
cat wonder
due
once
days 30 37
roles A
when is A ow_garden
when var garden >= 3
text {A} opens the fleet channel and turns the camera on the tray. In the last pod, a pale hook of a shoot has split the seed coat and turned, against no gravity at all, toward the lamp. Six ships screenshot it at once.
do morale A 6

card c_garden
type beat
cat human
due
once
days 37 38
roles A
when is A ow_garden
when fired p_garden_sprout
text The entry checklist says loose items go in the locker. {A} reads it, puts the seedling's tray in the locker, and takes it straight back out. One cargo strap later it rides beside the seat. "It comes with me," {A} tells the flight surgeon, who has stopped arguing.
do morale A 3

card p_garden_none
type beat
cat grim
due
once
days 37 37
roles A
when is A ow_garden
when !fired p_garden_sprout
text Rationed water was one squeeze too many: the last pod never came up. {A} keeps watering the tray, two millilitres, on schedule, and packs the dry seed in a coat pocket for the ground. Seeds are patient. So, it turns out, is {A}.
do trait A warm 2

# --- The middle dark ------------------------------------------------------------
card w_venus_shadow
type event
cat wonder
days 7 18
weight 6
once
roles A
when cond A ok
text With the cabin lights off, the Sun behind the hull and the shutters open, {A}'s hand throws a shadow on the bulkhead, so faint {A} has to move the hand to see it. The light source is Venus. {A} makes a rabbit, then a fist, then an open hand, letting the planet cast it.
do trait A curious 3

card w_phosphene
type beat
once
cat grim
days 19 23
weight 6
roles A
when cond A ok
text {A} shuts both eyes in the bunk and sees a white spark, then another. Cosmic rays, passing straight through the eye, fast enough to make light; cameras see them too, as single bright pixels. {A} counts them like sheep and loses count somewhere in the twenties.
do trait A curious 2
do morale A -1

card l_crystals
type event
cat grim
once
weight 40
days 20 28
roles A
when cond A ok
when home A
text The protein-crystal experiment in {A}'s locker, a university lab's two years of work, cooks overnight when its freezer fan seizes. {A} reads the temperature trace, then calls the lab, who ask for photos anyway. There is no second batch, and no second flight for it.
do morale A -3

card w_comet
type event
cat wonder
days 20 30
weight 6
once
roles A
when cond A ok
when home A
text The magnetometer on {A}'s ship twitches for six hours: the fleet is crossing the ion tail of a comet that last came this way before anyone aboard was born. There's nothing to see. {A} sits by the window anyway, with the trace scrolling on a tablet.
do trait A curious 3
do morale A 2

card p_birthday
type beat
cat life
days 8 39
weight 7
once
roles A B
when same A B
when !fired beat_haircut
when away A
when home B
text It's {B}'s birthday by the ground calendar, and {A} is still aboard from the last crossing. {A} produces a candle that can't be lit, a cake that is a ration bar with a slice of dried mango on it, and a card signed by the whole fleet. {B} keeps the candle.
do bond A B 6
do morale B 5

card p_movie
type beat
cat life
days 7 39
weight 7
once
roles A B
when same A B
text Movie night with {B}, on a tablet stuck to the ceiling: {A} picked a film set on a submarine. Halfway through, the hull ticks as the ship turns out of the sun. {A} pauses it, and the two of them listen until it stops. Then {A} puts on something with a sky in it.
do bond A B 4

card p_dream
type beat
once
cat human
days 10 39
weight 5
roles A
when cond A ok
text {A} wakes from a dream of rain on a car roof and lies still, trying to keep the sound. The fans hum. The ship ticks as it turns into the sun. By breakfast the rain has gone. {A} writes "rain, car roof" in the log margin, in case it comes back.
do morale A -2
do trait A warm 2

card l_long_table
type event
cat life
due
once
days 7 7
roles A
when cond A ok
text Once a week the fleet eats together on video: seven tablets on seven galley tables, one meal at one time. {A} is in charge of the toast. It's short, it isn't a joke, and it lands.
do morale A 3

card l_long_table2
type event
cat life
days 26 38
weight 6
once
roles A B
when cond A ok
when is A ow_list
when cond B ok
text Long table night. {B} has the toast and gives it to the empty chair at each of the seven tables, the one where a second crew member would sit on a normal ship. It lands on every screen at once, the one conversation out here with no delay in it. {A} laughs on the beat, and it counts double.
do morale A 3

card g_third_quarter
type event
cat grim
days 27 34
weight 9
once
roles A B
when cond A ok
when cond B ok
when !is B ow_list
text The flight surgeon calls it the third-quarter effect. On the video link {A} and {B} find themselves on the same checklist page at the same minute, both stuck on step four. {A} reads the steps aloud, the way they would on a pass, and {B} answers each one. They file a ticket: the page is too long.
do bond A B 6
do morale B 3

card g_count
type beat
cat grim
days 18 39
weight 5
once
roles A
when cond A ok
text {A} counts the medical kit against the manifest: sutures, splints, pain tablets in neat blister rows. {A} counts it once more and closes the lid gently.
do trait A brave 2

card g_packer
type event
cat human
due
once
days 28 28
roles A
text A batch of photos from the Starbase loading crew reaches {A}: the bay, the cranes, the team in hi-vis, a named forklift charging off a cargo ship's landing leg. The one with the Sharpie signs off: "Seven of you this time. Write when you land." {A} clips the forklift inside the logbook.
do morale A 2

card sharpie2
type beat
cat human
days 26 39
weight 12
once
roles A
when fired dil_stash
when cond A ok
text Under the last tray in the spares locker, {A} finds a roll of tape that isn't on any list, and under it a laminated card in a bag: an old handshake procedure, headed in the same Sharpie hand: "Old manners, for old hardware." Beside it, the little ship again, fingers crossed.
do res spares 1
do morale A 5

# --- The approach --------------------------------------------------------------
card w_aurora
type event
cat wonder
days 33 39
weight 9
once
roles A
when cond A ok
text In one of the orbiters' night frames {A} finds a faint green smear over dark ground: Martian aurora, patchy, pinned to old magnetized rock no hand has ever touched. {A} saves the frame and sends it to the geology team, subject line: "look".
do trait A curious 3

card w_phobos
type event
cat wonder
days 37 39
weight 14
once
roles A
when cond A ok
text Phobos is a speck beside Mars on the long-lens camera now, crossing its face in under an hour. {A} watches it cross a whole world in the time it takes to eat a meal, and wants weight, suddenly, more than sleep.
do trait A curious 2
do morale A 3

card w_mars_disc
type event
cat arrival
due
once
days 41 41
roles A
when flag c2_answered
when !is A ow_hail
text {A} holds a thumb up to the window, the old Earth-watch habit. Mars still fits behind it, for a few more nights: three parts rust, one part dark, the dawn line curved along one edge. Just past that line, too small to see, a light is holding steady.
do morale A 5

card w_mars_disc_q
type event
cat arrival
due
once
days 41 41
roles A
when !flag c2_answered
when !is A ow_hail
text {A} holds a thumb up to the window, the old Earth-watch habit. Mars still fits behind it, for a few more nights: three parts rust, one part dark, the dawn line curved along one edge. Just past that line, too small to see, a light is keeping time.
do morale A 5

card a_last_night
type beat
cat arrival
due
once
days 41 41
roles A B
when is A ow_dose
when !flag arrive_wait
text The last nights before entry. {A} checks the water tanks that shielded the bunk all these weeks, by hand, the way you'd pat a horse. On the fleet channel {B} is doing the same on another ship. "Same time tomorrow?" {B} asks. "On the ground," {A} says. "One way or the other." {B} sets an alarm for it.
do bond A B 6

card a_last_night_o
type beat
cat arrival
due
once
days 41 41
roles A B
when is A ow_dose
when flag arrive_wait
text The last nights before aerocapture. {A} checks the water tanks that shielded the bunk all these weeks, by hand, the way you'd pat a horse. On the fleet channel {B} is doing the same on another ship. "Same time tomorrow?" {B} asks. "In orbit," {A} says. "Then the ground. Then we'll see."
do bond A B 6

# --- Arrival day: what the fleet chose, and what it cost ------------------------------
card a_recall_home
type event
cat arrival
due
once
days 40 40
roles A
when fired m_reveal
when flag name_home
text On the new pass {A} finds the crater the fleet named for a small town at home, and Cargo 2 behind its rim, where no old map could show it. Somewhere on Earth, a town newspaper is about to need a second front page.

card a_recall_plan
type event
cat arrival
due
once
days 40 40
roles A
when fired m_reveal
when flag name_plan
text On the new pass {A} finds the crater the fleet named for the first person who ever wrote a Mars plan, and Cargo 2 behind its rim, where no old map could show it. Somewhere on Earth, a committee is about to have a great deal more to argue about.

card a_recall_photo
type event
cat arrival
due
once
days 38 38
roles A
when flag photo_taken
text {A} stows the tablet with the fleet portrait on it: six ships and the edge of a seventh, Earth behind them, and the propellant it took to fly them that close, which would have been nice to have for the descent. Worth it, {A} decides.

card a_recall_wrist
type event
cat arrival
due
once
days 37 37
roles A
when fired crisis_eva
when is A eva_who
text {A} runs the first entry seat checks with the wrist that wouldn't bend, mostly bending now, and reports it to the flight surgeon as "bending", with the angle in degrees. The surgeon clears the seat.

card a_recall_valve
type event
cat arrival
due
once
days 39 39
roles A
when flag valve_out
when is A valve_who
when !is A abort_who
text Before the descent brief {A} flies the valve workaround once more in the simulator, one thruster short. The model rolls the wrong way out of the blackout and comes back, the way it did that night. {A} initials the log line and closes the panel.

card a_recall_shared
type event
cat arrival
due
once
days 40 40
roles A B
when flag stash_exposed
when is A stash_who
when !is B stash_b
text {A} sent {B} the last pack from the locker on the last crossing, with a note on the bag in borrowed handwriting: "You'll thank me." {B} opens it tonight.
do bond B A 3

card a_recall_marker
type event
cat arrival
due
once
days 41 41
roles A
when is A ow_theory
text {A} uncaps the blue marker one last time and adds a second lighthouse to the drawing: small, standing on the ground, and beside it a figure holding a Sharpie. Then {A} folds it into a chest pocket with the marker.
do morale A 2

card a_suit_plan
type event
cat arrival
due
once
days 42 42
roles A
when flag signal_ignored
when is A ow_hail
when cond A ok
text {A} packs a handheld radio into a suit thigh pocket, retuned to the old channel, the old program key loaded by the ground, a procedure card with two signatures clipped to the back. "First one out goes to say hello," {A} tells the ground. The ground, which asked for a suit beside it, says yes.
do morale A 3

# --- Day 42: the entry itself, last on the page; one scene per arrival branch, told by whoever was drilled on taking the landing by hand.
card e_entry_hold
type event
cat arrival
due
once
days 42 42
roles A
when flag arrive_hold
when flag c2_answered
when is A abort_who
text Entry interface. Four minutes of plasma blackout, seven ships silent in turn. Below twenty kilometres the cameras see only brown. {A}'s ship slews in a gust the model never had. The radar has had the ground since eight kilometres; Cargo 2's ping holds the bearing. At three hundred metres the brown thins and a slope comes up under the ship; {A} calls the manual takeover before the plume takes the view.
do morale A 3

card e_entry_hold_q
type event
cat arrival
due
once
days 42 42
roles A
when flag arrive_hold
when !flag c2_answered
when is A abort_who
text Entry interface. Four minutes of plasma blackout, seven ships silent in turn. From twenty kilometres down the cameras see only brown. {A}'s ship slews in a gust the model never had. The radar has had the ground since eight kilometres. At three hundred metres the cameras find a slope under the ship; {A} calls the manual takeover before the plume takes the view, and fights it level. It comes down hard, upright.
do morale A 3

card e_entry_wait
type event
cat arrival
due
once
days 42 42
roles A
when flag arrive_wait
when is A abort_who
text Aerocapture. Four minutes of plasma blackout, seven ships silent in turn. Six come out the far side on time. {A}'s comes out eleven seconds late: eleven seconds of nothing on the fleet channel, the call for a manual corridor correction ready on {A}'s tongue. Then {A}'s voice, reading out the orbit numbers as if nothing happened.
do morale A 3

card e_entry_clear
type event
cat arrival
due
once
days 42 42
roles A
when !flag arrive_hold
when !flag arrive_wait
when is A abort_who
text Entry interface in clear air. Four minutes of plasma blackout, seven ships silent in turn. At the landing burn one of {A}'s engines lights late, a long half second, and the engine-out call is half out of {A}'s mouth when it catches. The ground comes up exactly where the maps said.
do morale A 3

card w_zodiac
type event
cat wonder
days 8 20
weight 10
once
roles A
when cond A ok
text With the cabin dark and the Sun behind the hull, {A} sees the zodiacal light with no air in the way: a long faint cone of comet dust, lit from behind. From home it is a smudge at dusk. Out here it is a road. {A} turns the screen brightness down to keep it.
do morale A 3

card w_sun_small
type event
cat wonder
days 24 33
weight 10
once
roles A
when cond A ok
text Through the shade filter the Sun is a coin held further off each week. The solar arrays say it first, a percent or two less on every page. {A} turns the cabin heater up a notch, and caps the filter on a star that used to be a sky.
do morale A 2

card w_milky
type event
cat wonder
days 20 20
due
once
roles A
when cond A ok
text {A} kills every cabin light, shades the Sun-side window and waits twenty minutes for night eyes. The Milky Way comes up with the dark lanes in it, the ones no backyard ever shows. {A} names the ones in the book, then starts on the rest.
do trait A curious 2

card w_moon_pair
type event
cat wonder
days 22 22
due
once
roles A
when cond A ok
text Through the long lens Earth and the Moon fit in one frame now, a blue dot and a grey one, close as two buttons on a coat. {A} shoots the pair once a shift for a week and sends the frames home as a flipbook, captioned "You are here. Both of you."
do morale A 3
